33. Qa8+ Ke7 34. Qxa6 Qc1 35. Qa3+ Kf6 36. Qc3 Kg7 37. f4 Rd1 38. Qxe5+ (38.
Ke2 $1 $11) 38... Kh7 39. Ne3 Rd2+ 40. Kf3 Qh1+ {"Mr. Madgavkar resigned,
though the reason of the resignation lies not on the surface, for no forced
win for Black is obvious, and, as the resignation came just a few minutes
before the call of time, the adjudicator would have had a difficult task to
demonstrate a win." (BCM, May 1892, p196) Additional sources: The Field, 16 April
1892; Chess Monthly, May 1892 and CN 3193} (40... Qh1+ 41. Kg4 {and analysis
engines find} Rd6 $3 $19 ({The Field, 16 April 1892, gives} 41... f5+ {as the
winning move, but doesn't consider} 42. Kg5 {after which there is no
demonstrable win.})) 0-1

